WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.420
Many of us REMEMBER things for exams because

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.520
we learn them without context.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.180
And, to learn without context is what we call

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.380
rote learning.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.700
So what if I told you that you don’t need

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.980
to remember things?

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.600
It’s possible if we try to understand the

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.900
core concepts!

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.360
And to learn or to understand, we need to

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.300
first start by asking the right questions.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.500
For example, instead of asking ‘WHY are

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.360
there no real humans in Don't memorise videos’,

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.420
we could ask, ‘WHO are the humans behind

00:00:36.427 --> 00:00:37.420
these videos?

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:45.320
Hey guys, my name is Zarina and I am the voice

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.260
behind all the videos that you see on this

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.100
channel.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.315
We have an army of animators, illustrators

00:00:51.315 --> 00:00:53.880
and educators who help us create them.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.880
And, it all began with Ganesh and Rohan

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:58.180
Hi! I’m Ganesh.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:59.700
Hi, I’m Rohan.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.880
Let me begin by telling you why I started

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.800
Don't Memorise. A few years ago I told my dad that I want

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.880
to be a teacher and I want to teach hundreds

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.540
of students over the next five years.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.780
To which he replied “Hundreds isn’t cool

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.020
you know what’s cool?

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.020
“millions”?

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:16.920
And, that's why I started this YouTube channel.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.674
And I decided to join him in this journey,

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.120
because I strongly believe in the company’s

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.590
goal to be the BEST TEACHERS out there.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:26.203
We make videos ranging from school level math

00:01:26.203 --> 00:01:28.700
and science to test prep content, and we’ve

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.840
started adding some brain teaser videos as well.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.660
We believe that true learning not just helps

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.760
you in your exams but in your real life too!

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.900
So we asked each other “how would we define

00:01:37.919 --> 00:01:38.710
real success”?

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:41.080
If a million students end up saying, 'I’ve

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.960
become a better person because of Don't Memorise',

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.540
that would mean real success for us.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.525
Finally, we would like to thank all of you

00:01:46.525 --> 00:01:48.840
for watching our videos, giving us your feedback,

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.120
and participating in our contests.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.640
If you feel that there are others who could

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.500
benefit from our content, don't forget to

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.270
share our videos with them.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:58.360
And as always, do share your thoughts with

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.360
us in the comments section below.

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:01.860
We love to hear from you.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:04.200
To subscribe to our channel, click on the

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.660
atom you see here.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.490
And to watch an interesting video, click on

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:08.720
the Newton’s cradle there.

